# Local, read-only, version-aware: one line leaves the machine.
flow
  columns 1,1,0.9
  gap 120,40
title "One line leaves the machine"
description "The MCP client asks the TYPO3 Support App subprocess, which draws its answers from bundled knowledge and from the project's own packages and installation — all inside the developer's machine. One read-only path crosses the boundary to fetch from official documentation and core services; nothing is written back across it."

group machine "your machine"
  client "MCP-enabled client"
    at 0,0
    span 2
    body "Starts one local PHP subprocess over stdio."
  app "TYPO3 Support App"
    at 0,1
    span 2
    body "Routes by task, version and scope. Read-only, except feedback you ask for explicitly."
    ink
  knowledge `bundled knowledge`
    at 0,2
    body "Curated, version-bound."
  packages `packages & installation`
    at 1,2
    body "What this checkout supplies."
group outside "outside"
  docs `docs.typo3.org`
    at 2,1
    body "Canonical documentation."
    absent
  core `core services`
    at 2,2
    body "Live registries and APIs."
    absent

client <-> app "question · answer"
knowledge -> app
packages -> app
outside => app "read-only"
  via h
